Odin (ᚨ), Copyright (C) 2026 Réda Chérif-Touil
Released under the GNU GPL, version 3 or later (see LICENSE).

Odin emulates two arcade systems, for Linux, Windows and macOS, drawing with
OpenGL or Vulkan:

 SEGA Hikaru       low-level, running the real chips' programs where known
 Gaelco ATV Track  low-level too, the Neon 250's microcoded core running its
                   own code (its 3D drawn from the scene it builds)

Odin runs the six Hikaru games, two of them in two versions, and the Gaelco
games. They play with a keyboard, gamepads, wheels with force feedback
(NASCAR, ATV Track, Smashing Drive) or light guns (Brave Firefighters).
Virtual-On saves to its card.
Odin links cabinets over the network and sends the cabinet outputs as MAME
does.


GAMES
=====

SEGA Hikaru
 airtrix    Air Trix
 airtrixo   Air Trix (original)
 braveff    Brave Firefighters
 pharrier   Planet Harriers
 sgnascar   NASCAR Arcade
 sgnascaro  NASCAR Arcade (original)
 swracer    Star Wars Racer Arcade
 von4       Cyber Troopers Virtual-On Force

Gaelco ATV Track (see INSTALL)
 atvtrack   ATV Track
 atvtracka  ATV Track (set 2)
 gfootbal   Gaelco Football
 smashdrv   Smashing Drive
 smashdrvb  Smashing Drive (UK)
 smashdrvs  Smashing Drive (Spain, Portugal)


Each name is a MAME set. The Hikaru games also need the shared sets hikaru
and mie; jvs13551, 18wheelr and srally2 are optional.

The title screens and bezels of the games come in a separate pack,
Odin-Artwork.zip, released with Odin: extract it beside the program. All
rights to these pictures are reserved by SEGA.

INSTALL tells how to build and start Odin, OPTIONS lists every option and
setting, TODO what is missing or guessed.

The three Gaelco games use Odin's controls. In Gaelco Football the right
stick kicks: pull it back first to lift the ball.


REPORTING A PROBLEM
===================

Ask for help in the Arcade Community Discord: https://arcade.community
Report a bug of Odin on GitHub: https://github.com/Tovarichtch/Odin/issues

Odin writes what it does to odin.log, in its folder (see FILES in INSTALL),
at each start; the start before is kept as odin-previous.log. When
something goes wrong, send odin.log (and odin-previous.log after a crash)
with your report: what you did, which game, which computer.

If we ask for more: turn on the detailed log (page Paths, Detailed log, or
the bar, DEBUG), start the game again and send the new odin.log. It makes
the game much slower and the file much bigger: turn it off afterwards.


CREDITS
=======

Odin is a hard fork of Valkyrie, the Hikaru emulator by Stefano Teso,
Copyright (C) 2011-2013, GNU GPL version 3 or later.
The ATV Track board follows MAME's atvtrack driver; its boot program stays
under the BSD-3-Clause licence, Copyright (c) Samuele Zannoli.

Daniel Martin (dmanlfc) contributed to Odin and brought it the Gaelco
boards: ATV Track, Gaelco Football and Smashing Drive.

Thanks to the developers of MAME (its Hikaru driver) and Flycast, and to
Neill Corlett for his documentation of the AICA.

Odin also uses Dear ImGui, SDL 3, GLEW, Jansson, Vulkan-Headers, miniz,
the LZMA SDK, the Lola Retro CRT filters, the Cozette and Junicode fonts
and AL2009man's gamepad drawings. Their licences are on the page About of
the menu and beside their sources.
